      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Column-to-Port Binding (Pack / Unpack)\n\n**Dataset Unpack** turns a `DATASET` into one output port per column (`x0`..`x3` plus the `target`); **Dataset Pack** stacks per-column tensor ports back into a table — the port name *is* the column name (stamp it by connecting from an Unpack port, or rename the slot). The number of ports follows the table schema, so feature-engineering branches can consume individual columns.\n\nThis demo unpacks a 500-row synthetic table, repacks it (port `target` becomes the label again), and previews the head. Run it once: the Unpack node's ports are (re)built from the real schema and persist with the saved workflow."
      ],
      "title": "How this works"
    },
